cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "RAGSec: A Layered Defense Framework for Retrieval-Augmented Generation Under Adaptive Knowledge Poisoning"
message: "If you use this software or its results, please cite the accompanying article."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Islam
    given-names: Md Mazharul
    email: mazharul.islam1@northsouth.edu
    affiliation: North South University
repository-code: "https://github.com/mazharulmd/ragsec"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - retrieval-augmented generation
  - knowledge poisoning
  - prompt injection
  - adaptive adversary
  - data provenance
  - large language models
  - AI supply chain security
abstract: >-
  An instrumented retrieval-augmented generation framework with four independently
  switchable defense layers (ingestion-time source verification, calibrated retrieval
  filtering, provenance-weighted robust aggregation and anomaly monitoring), five
  knowledge-base poisoning attacks including a defense-aware adaptive adversary with six
  individually switchable evasion techniques, and a reproducible experiment suite that
  attributes defensive failure to specific adversary capabilities.
